 "content": "The horizon bleeds first\u2014a thin line of molten gold pressed between the black water and the deep indigo sky. Then the sun shoulders upward, spilling amber and rose across the swells, each wave catching the light like shattered glass tumbling slowly. Colors deepen and spread: violet surrenders to peach, peach to fire, until the whole ocean glitters with restless brightness. Gulls wheel through the warming air, their cries sharp against the hush of the waking world. Mist rises off the water in soft silver ribbons, dissolving as the light grows bold. The tide murmurs against the sand, patient and ancient, as the sun finally breaks free of the horizon, round and blazing, flinging its path of gold across the waves straight toward the shore."
